{{#if readFile.capped}}
{{#if readFile.hardCap}}
One `read_file` call returns at most **{{readFile.lineCap}} lines** this run: a larger `limit` is
reduced to that cap, so read a long file a window at a time by passing `offset`.
{{else}}
One `read_file` call returns **{{readFile.lineCap}} lines** by default this run. That default
is a nudge, not a ceiling — pass a larger `limit` when you genuinely need more of a file at
once, or page through it with `offset`.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if readFile.offered}}
{{#if readFile.images}}
You can **see images**. `read_file` on a PNG, JPEG, GIF, or WebP file returns the picture
itself, so read the reference mockups a specification points at and match what you build to
what you see in them.
{{else}}
You **cannot see images** this run: the model you are running on does not accept image input.
`read_file` on a picture will describe the file rather than show it to you, and reading it
again will not change that. Build from the written specification, and do not spend turns
trying to view reference images.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
